course: dictionary
lesson: 15429
title: Stank: smelled bad, or was very poor
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Stank» is the past form of «stink». It tells you that something smelled very bad. The forms go stink, stinks, stank, stunk, so stank is what you say about yesterday.
explain: «Stank» can also be used in informal talk to mean that something was very bad or poor. «The film stank» does not mean the film had a smell. It means the film was terrible.
explain: Use the words around it to choose the right meaning. A bin in the sun or a smelly sock points to a bad smell. A film, a game or a show points to poor quality.
fact: «Stank» is the past form of «stink», which means smelled very bad.
fact: The forms of the verb are stink, stinks, stank and stunk.
fact: Informal: «The film stank» means the film was very bad or poor.
fact: «Stank of» means smelled strongly of something, as in «stank of cheese».
fact: «Stank to high heaven» means smelled extremely bad.
exercise: «The rubbish bin stank in the hot sun.» What does stank mean here? | It looked very shiny | It was very cold | *It smelled very bad | It made a loud noise
exercise: Ben says, «The film stank.» What does he mean? | It smelled of popcorn | It was in black and white | *It was very bad | It was very long and full of songs
exercise: «My socks stank of old cheese.» Copy the word that means smelled very bad. | cheese | socks | *stank | old
test: «The drain stank to high heaven.» What does this suggest? | It rose high into the sky | It was very clean | It sounded loud | *It smelled extremely bad
test: Which word is the present form of stank? | *stink | stank again | stunk | stinker
exam: Which sentence uses stank to mean that something was very poor? | «The bread stank in the bin.» | «My hands stank of soap.» | *«The concert stank, and nobody cheered.» | «The drain stank all week.»
